{
 "fps": 30,
 "total": 19839,
 "xf": 18,
 "titleAfter": 5,
 "shots": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_01.jpg",
   "start": 0,
   "end": 336,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Imagine a bright white light, brighter than the sun, over a city of tens of thousands. Seconds later, a wall of heat and wind. Nothing is left standing.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s01.mp3",
     "dur": 10.128,
     "start": 10,
     "end": 314
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_02.jpg",
   "start": 318,
   "end": 746,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "That is the story told about this hill in Jordan, called Tall el-Hammam. A comet blast, three and a half thousand years ago. A real Bronze Age city, wiped out. Possibly even Sodom.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s02.mp3",
     "dur": 13.2,
     "start": 328,
     "end": 724
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "D",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_03.jpg",
   "start": 728,
   "end": 1074,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And in two thousand twenty-one, a respected journal published a paper that said it was proven. Then, in two thousand twenty-five, that same journal pulled it back.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s03.mp3",
     "dur": 10.464,
     "start": 738,
     "end": 1052
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_04.jpg",
   "start": 1056,
   "end": 1376,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "So tonight we sit at the retraction desk. We take the claim apart line by line, and we mark every line: evidence, theory, or debunked.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s04.mp3",
     "dur": 9.576,
     "start": 1066,
     "end": 1354
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_05.jpg",
   "start": 1358,
   "end": 1691,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "First, the site itself. Because the real story is stranger than the headline. Case open.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s05.mp3",
     "dur": 6.024,
     "start": 1368,
     "end": 1549
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "I \u00b7 THE SITE",
    "A Hill Called Hot Baths",
    "JORDAN VALLEY"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_06.jpg",
   "start": 1673,
   "end": 1993,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter one. The site. Tall el-Hammam lies in the Jordan Valley, east of the river, about thirteen kilometres northeast of the Dead Sea.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s06.mp3",
     "dur": 9.576,
     "start": 1683,
     "end": 1971
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_07.jpg",
   "start": 1975,
   "end": 2285,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The mound is huge. The fortified city covered about twenty-six hectares, and the upper part of the hill stands roughly thirty metres high.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s07.mp3",
     "dur": 9.264,
     "start": 1985,
     "end": 2263
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_08.jpg",
   "start": 2267,
   "end": 2609,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "People lived here for thousands of years. From the Chalcolithic, about four thousand BC, through the Iron Age, and into Roman and Byzantine times.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s08.mp3",
     "dur": 10.32,
     "start": 2277,
     "end": 2587
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_09.jpg",
   "start": 2591,
   "end": 2976,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "But the city was biggest during the Middle Bronze Age, around two thousand to sixteen hundred BC. At that time it was one of the largest settlements in the whole region.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s09.mp3",
     "dur": 11.736,
     "start": 2601,
     "end": 2954
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_10.jpg",
   "start": 2958,
   "end": 3232,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The name means Hill of the Hot Baths. In twenty eleven, diggers found a Byzantine bath, which fits the name beautifully.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s10.mp3",
     "dur": 8.064,
     "start": 2968,
     "end": 3210
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 11,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "C",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_11.jpg",
   "start": 3214,
   "end": 3529,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The American scholar Nelson Glueck surveyed the valley in nineteen forty-one. He tied this area to a biblical place called Abel Shittim.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s11.mp3",
     "dur": 9.408,
     "start": 3224,
     "end": 3507
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 12,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_12.jpg",
   "start": 3511,
   "end": 3878,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Real excavation began in the nineteen seventies. Then from two thousand five to two thousand sixteen, a team led by Steven Collins dug here every season.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s12.mp3",
     "dur": 11.136,
     "start": 3521,
     "end": 3856
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_13.jpg",
   "start": 3860,
   "end": 4147,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And Collins argued something bold. This was not just any city. It was Sodom, the city destroyed in the book of Genesis.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s13.mp3",
     "dur": 8.496,
     "start": 3870,
     "end": 4125
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 14,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_14.jpg",
   "start": 4129,
   "end": 4468,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Mainstream archaeologists rejected that. So did many other biblical scholars. But a theory needs a destroyed city, so let us look at the destruction.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s14.mp3",
     "dur": 10.224,
     "start": 4139,
     "end": 4446
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 15,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "II \u00b7 THE LAYER",
    "What They Found",
    "TRENCH \u00b7 BRONZE AGE"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_15.jpg",
   "start": 4450,
   "end": 4763,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter two. The destruction layer. In the trenches, the diggers found a dark band of burnt material, with broken pottery and collapsed mudbrick.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s15.mp3",
     "dur": 9.36,
     "start": 4460,
     "end": 4741
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_16.jpg",
   "start": 4745,
   "end": 4973,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Some of the pottery looked glassy on the outside, as if it had been heated far beyond a normal fire.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s16.mp3",
     "dur": 6.528,
     "start": 4755,
     "end": 4951
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 17,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_17.jpg",
   "start": 4955,
   "end": 5214,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Some walls had collapsed in a single direction. And, the team said, the upper part of the settlement had been stripped away.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s17.mp3",
     "dur": 7.56,
     "start": 4965,
     "end": 5192
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 18,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_18.jpg",
   "start": 5196,
   "end": 5471,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "After that, the area seems to have been abandoned for hundreds of years. A real gap in the story, which happens to matter later.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s18.mp3",
     "dur": 8.088,
     "start": 5206,
     "end": 5449
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 19,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_19.jpg",
   "start": 5453,
   "end": 5827,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "In two thousand twenty-one, the team published their explanation in Scientific Reports. The title spoke of a Bronze Age city destroyed by a cosmic airburst.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s19.mp3",
     "dur": 11.4,
     "start": 5463,
     "end": 5805
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 20,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_20.jpg",
   "start": 5809,
   "end": 6171,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The evidence they listed was microscopic. Tiny melted grains, called spherules. Shocked quartz. Zircon crystals that looked heated to extreme temperatures.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s20.mp3",
     "dur": 10.992,
     "start": 5819,
     "end": 6149
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 21,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_21.jpg",
   "start": 6153,
   "end": 6476,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Their picture: a small comet fragment explodes in the air, like Tunguska, nineteen oh eight, and the blast and heat destroy everything below.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s21.mp3",
     "dur": 9.672,
     "start": 6163,
     "end": 6454
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 22,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_22.jpg",
   "start": 6458,
   "end": 6745,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "They claimed temperatures above two thousand degrees Celsius. Hot enough to melt rock, and to turn ordinary pottery to glass.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s22.mp3",
     "dur": 8.472,
     "start": 6468,
     "end": 6723
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 23,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_23.jpg",
   "start": 6727,
   "end": 7005,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "It is a gripping story. A one-off, instant, city-killing blast, ending in a salt-crusted wasteland. So who checked it?",
     "file": "ep/audio/s23.mp3",
     "dur": 8.184,
     "start": 6737,
     "end": 6983
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 24,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "III \u00b7 THE REVIEW",
    "Who Checked",
    "PEER SCRUTINY"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_24.jpg",
   "start": 6987,
   "end": 7208,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter three. The review. Because science is not what a paper says. It is what survives afterwards.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s24.mp3",
     "dur": 6.288,
     "start": 6997,
     "end": 7186
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 25,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_25.jpg",
   "start": 7190,
   "end": 7540,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Start with who wrote it. A large share of the authors belonged to the Comet Research Group, a body which sponsors the idea that comets repeatedly struck Earth.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s25.mp3",
     "dur": 10.584,
     "start": 7200,
     "end": 7518
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_26.jpg",
   "start": 7522,
   "end": 7781,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "That does not make them wrong. But it does mean the airburst was a thesis they had been defending long before this dig.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s26.mp3",
     "dur": 7.536,
     "start": 7532,
     "end": 7759
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 27,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "D",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_27.jpg",
   "start": 7763,
   "end": 8091,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Next, the outside experts. The physicist Mark Boslough, whose own work is cited in the paper, said the paper's reading of his models was wrong.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s27.mp3",
     "dur": 9.84,
     "start": 7773,
     "end": 8069
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 28,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "D",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_28.jpg",
   "start": 8073,
   "end": 8368,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Then came the images. The scientific-integrity researcher Elisabeth Bik showed that some figures in the paper had been altered.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s28.mp3",
     "dur": 8.76,
     "start": 8083,
     "end": 8346
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 29,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "D",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_29.jpg",
   "start": 8350,
   "end": 8608,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "In March twenty twenty-two, an independent review concluded that the criteria for an airburst were simply not met.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s29.mp3",
     "dur": 7.512,
     "start": 8360,
     "end": 8586
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 30,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_30.jpg",
   "start": 8590,
   "end": 8970,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Questions piled up. Were the melted grains from the destruction layer, or just from ordinary fires and dirt? Were the temperatures real, or estimated from an assumption?",
     "file": "ep/audio/s30.mp3",
     "dur": 11.568,
     "start": 8600,
     "end": 8948
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 31,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "D",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_31.jpg",
   "start": 8952,
   "end": 9224,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "In February twenty twenty-three, the journal added an editor's note, warning readers that the conclusions were under question.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s31.mp3",
     "dur": 7.992,
     "start": 8962,
     "end": 9202
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 32,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "D",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_32.jpg",
   "start": 9206,
   "end": 9601,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And on the twenty-fourth of April, twenty twenty-five, Scientific Reports retracted the paper. Reason: concerns about methodology, analysis and data interpretation.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s32.mp3",
     "dur": 12.072,
     "start": 9216,
     "end": 9579
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 33,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "IV \u00b7 THE GROUND",
    "What Is Left",
    "SOLID FINDS"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_33.jpg",
   "start": 9583,
   "end": 9795,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter four. What the ground really says. Strip away the airburst, and what is left? Quite a lot.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s33.mp3",
     "dur": 6.0,
     "start": 9593,
     "end": 9773
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 34,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_34.jpg",
   "start": 9777,
   "end": 10067,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Tall el-Hammam was a major walled city, with huge ramparts and a large population. That is fact, dug out of the earth.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s34.mp3",
     "dur": 8.592,
     "start": 9787,
     "end": 10045
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 35,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_35.jpg",
   "start": 10049,
   "end": 10379,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Something did end that city, or at least reduced it. Burnt layers are real. Many ancient cities were burned by war, earthquake or accident.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s35.mp3",
     "dur": 9.912,
     "start": 10059,
     "end": 10357
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 36,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_36.jpg",
   "start": 10361,
   "end": 10669,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Mudbrick cities burn easily. Roofs held timber and reeds. A siege, or a single bad night, can fill a trench with black ash.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s36.mp3",
     "dur": 9.168,
     "start": 10371,
     "end": 10647
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 37,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_37.jpg",
   "start": 10651,
   "end": 10934,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The valley also sits on the Dead Sea Transform, a major fault line. Earthquakes here are not a theory, they are a certainty.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s37.mp3",
     "dur": 8.352,
     "start": 10661,
     "end": 10912
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 38,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_38.jpg",
   "start": 10916,
   "end": 11175,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Tilted walls and collapsed bricks are what you would expect after an earthquake, with fire after it. No comet needed.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s38.mp3",
     "dur": 7.56,
     "start": 10926,
     "end": 11153
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 39,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_39.jpg",
   "start": 11157,
   "end": 11439,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And the abandonment? Many sites in the valley show gaps. Drought, shifting trade routes and conquest can all empty a city.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s39.mp3",
     "dur": 8.304,
     "start": 11167,
     "end": 11417
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 40,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_40.jpg",
   "start": 11421,
   "end": 11655,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "That is the humbling part of archaeology. A gap tells us something happened. It never tells us what.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s40.mp3",
     "dur": 6.72,
     "start": 11431,
     "end": 11633
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 41,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_41.jpg",
   "start": 11637,
   "end": 11883,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "So the ground supports a great city and a burnt end. It does not, by itself, support a bomb from the sky.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s41.mp3",
     "dur": 7.128,
     "start": 11647,
     "end": 11861
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 42,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": [
    "V \u00b7 SODOM",
    "The Story Behind It",
    "GENESIS 19"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_42.jpg",
   "start": 11865,
   "end": 12108,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter five. The Sodom problem. The airburst claim was never just about science. It was about a story.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s42.mp3",
     "dur": 7.032,
     "start": 11875,
     "end": 12086
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 43,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "L",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_43.jpg",
   "start": 12090,
   "end": 12351,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Genesis tells of cities destroyed by fire and brimstone, and the Dead Sea region is where tradition places them.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s43.mp3",
     "dur": 7.632,
     "start": 12100,
     "end": 12329
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 44,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_44.jpg",
   "start": 12333,
   "end": 12669,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Plenty of places have been proposed. Some scholars say the cities lie beneath the southern Dead Sea. Others say Bab edh-Dhra. Collins says Hammam.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s44.mp3",
     "dur": 10.104,
     "start": 12343,
     "end": 12647
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 45,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_45.jpg",
   "start": 12651,
   "end": 12995,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The dates are one problem. Collins matched the destruction to the Middle Bronze Age, but the Genesis story is told, in tradition, about a different era.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s45.mp3",
     "dur": 10.392,
     "start": 12661,
     "end": 12973
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 46,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "L",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_46.jpg",
   "start": 12977,
   "end": 13277,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The geography is another. Texts place Sodom near the Dead Sea's plain, with the plain being called a circle, or kikkar, of the Jordan.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s46.mp3",
     "dur": 8.928,
     "start": 12987,
     "end": 13255
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 47,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "D",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_47.jpg",
   "start": 13259,
   "end": 13587,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "But nothing found at Hammam names it Sodom. No inscription, no seal, no text. The identification is an interpretation of a legend.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s47.mp3",
     "dur": 9.864,
     "start": 13269,
     "end": 13565
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 48,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_48.jpg",
   "start": 13569,
   "end": 13886,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "There is a modern cost, too. After the claim went viral, sites like this attract attention, and in the Middle East, attention can bring looters.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s48.mp3",
     "dur": 9.48,
     "start": 13579,
     "end": 13864
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 49,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_49.jpg",
   "start": 13868,
   "end": 14155,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Faith and archaeology can sit side by side. But when a dig is led by a conclusion, the data tends to bend toward it.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s49.mp3",
     "dur": 8.496,
     "start": 13878,
     "end": 14133
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 50,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_50.jpg",
   "start": 14137,
   "end": 14383,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "So can a real catastrophe still hide in the sand? Let us test the airburst idea on its own terms.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s50.mp3",
     "dur": 7.128,
     "start": 14147,
     "end": 14361
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 51,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "VI \u00b7 THE PHYSICS",
    "Can Air Burn Cities",
    "TUNGUSKA TEST"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_51.jpg",
   "start": 14365,
   "end": 14681,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter six. The physics. Airbursts are real. In nineteen oh eight, a blast flattened eighty million trees in Tunguska, Siberia.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s51.mp3",
     "dur": 9.456,
     "start": 14375,
     "end": 14659
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 52,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_52.jpg",
   "start": 14663,
   "end": 14997,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "In twenty thirteen, a smaller one burst over Chelyabinsk, Russia. The shockwave broke thousands of windows and injured over a thousand people.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s52.mp3",
     "dur": 10.056,
     "start": 14673,
     "end": 14975
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 53,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_53.jpg",
   "start": 14979,
   "end": 15253,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "But notice what those blasts did not do. They did not melt cities into glass, and they did not stay hot enough to bake pottery.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s53.mp3",
     "dur": 8.064,
     "start": 14989,
     "end": 15231
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 54,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "D",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_54.jpg",
   "start": 15235,
   "end": 15594,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Heat from an airburst lasts seconds. Melting thick mudbrick or sand takes time. The numbers in the paper needed a hotter, longer fire than physics allows.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s54.mp3",
     "dur": 10.896,
     "start": 15245,
     "end": 15572
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 55,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_55.jpg",
   "start": 15576,
   "end": 15897,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And ordinary fires, with timber roofs and olive oil, can reach surprisingly high heat. Some glassy slag is common in burnt cities.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s55.mp3",
     "dur": 9.624,
     "start": 15586,
     "end": 15875
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 56,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_56.jpg",
   "start": 15879,
   "end": 16213,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Spherules sound dramatic. But they rain constantly from space, and form from welding, volcanoes and lightning. Their presence alone proves little.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s56.mp3",
     "dur": 10.056,
     "start": 15889,
     "end": 16191
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 57,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_57.jpg",
   "start": 16195,
   "end": 16522,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Even the human story is thin. The paper described human remains, but critics said the evidence for a blast, rather than a collapse, is not clear.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s57.mp3",
     "dur": 9.816,
     "start": 16205,
     "end": 16500
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 58,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "D",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_58.jpg",
   "start": 16504,
   "end": 16791,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "No crater. No meteorite. No clear shocked rock. An airburst leaves clues, and these clues are missing or contested.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s58.mp3",
     "dur": 8.496,
     "start": 16514,
     "end": 16769
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 59,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "VII \u00b7 THE LESSON",
    "What A Retraction Means",
    "AFTER 2025"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_59.jpg",
   "start": 16773,
   "end": 17044,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter seven. The lessons. What does a retraction mean? It does not prove the opposite. It means the claim was not shown.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s59.mp3",
     "dur": 7.944,
     "start": 16783,
     "end": 17022
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 60,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_60.jpg",
   "start": 17026,
   "end": 17282,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The dig itself stands. The pottery, the walls, the ramparts: those are still real data that anyone can study.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s60.mp3",
     "dur": 7.44,
     "start": 17036,
     "end": 17260
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 61,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_61.jpg",
   "start": 17264,
   "end": 17490,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And the story is a warning. When we love a dramatic answer, we quietly lower the bar for proof.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s61.mp3",
     "dur": 6.456,
     "start": 17274,
     "end": 17468
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 62,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_62.jpg",
   "start": 17472,
   "end": 17630,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Which brings us to the scorecard. One at a time, claim by claim.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s62.mp3",
     "dur": 4.2,
     "start": 17482,
     "end": 17608
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 63,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_63.jpg",
   "start": 17612,
   "end": 17707,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Retraction desk, closing the file.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s63.mp3",
     "dur": 2.088,
     "start": 17622,
     "end": 17685
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 64,
   "fx": "score",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": [
    "VERDICT",
    "The Scorecard",
    "EVIDENCE VS THEORY"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_64.jpg",
   "start": 17689,
   "end": 17793,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The scorecard. Evidence against theory.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s64.mp3",
     "dur": 2.376,
     "start": 17699,
     "end": 17771
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 65,
   "fx": "score",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_65.jpg",
   "start": 17775,
   "end": 18183,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "A large Middle Bronze Age city at Hammam: evidence. A burnt end layer: partial. Earthquake and fire as explanation: plausible. Heat above two thousand degrees: doubtful.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s65.mp3",
     "dur": 12.528,
     "start": 17785,
     "end": 18161
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 66,
   "fx": "score",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_66.jpg",
   "start": 18165,
   "end": 18526,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The Genesis city of Sodom identified: unproven. The paper's airburst claim: retracted. A comet blast as alien disguise: no evidence at all.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s66.mp3",
     "dur": 10.944,
     "start": 18175,
     "end": 18504
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 67,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_67.jpg",
   "start": 18508,
   "end": 18817,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The verdict. A real city, a real mystery, but not a proven airburst. The most dramatic explanation turned out to be the weakest one.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s67.mp3",
     "dur": 9.216,
     "start": 18518,
     "end": 18795
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 68,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_68.jpg",
   "start": 18799,
   "end": 19133,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And the better story is that science worked. A bold claim was made, tested, challenged, and withdrawn. That is how the machine is supposed to run.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s68.mp3",
     "dur": 10.056,
     "start": 18809,
     "end": 19111
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 69,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_69.jpg",
   "start": 19115,
   "end": 19470,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Next case: the Hessdalen lights, a valley in Norway where strange glowing balls have been drifting over the hills for decades. Plasma, or something stranger?",
     "file": "ep/audio/s69.mp3",
     "dur": 10.752,
     "start": 19125,
     "end": 19448
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 70,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_70.jpg",
   "start": 19452,
   "end": 19764,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Do you think a catastrophe from the sky is still possible here? Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s70.mp3",
     "dur": 9.312,
     "start": 19462,
     "end": 19742
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}